/-!
# Foundations for generalized Jacobians

Divisor classes with full modulus congruences, their local-unit exact sequence,
and line bundles with chosen rigidifications. For a positive-degree modulus and
an ordinary pointed Poincaré family, the concrete frame quotient represents the
modulus Picard-zero group sheaf. Forgetting the modulus is the affine smooth
group projection with geometrically connected fibres. Its identity fibre is
the full scalar-unit quotient as a scheme, and its fppf group sheaf map is an
epimorphism. Compatibility of the kernel identification with group laws,
descent without a chosen section, and the remaining comparison theorems are separate.
-/
